WHAT
    Teach masm's WTF::systemPageSize() about wasi.

WHY
    src/3rdparty/masm/wtf/PageBlock.cpp defines systemPageSize() twice, once
    under OS(UNIX) and once under OS(WINDOWS), and on wasm neither is taken:
    masm's own Platform.h decides OS(UNIX) from a fixed list of system names
    plus `defined(unix)`, and wasi-sdk defines none of them. The build then
    fails in the one place that calls it:

        PageBlock.cpp:71:22: error: use of undeclared identifier 'systemPageSize'
           71 |         s_pageSize = systemPageSize();

    The UNIX implementation is `sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE)`, which wasi-libc
    provides and which answers 65536 -- the wasm linear-memory page, a power of
    two as pageSize()'s ASSERT requires. So the fix is to widen that one
    function's guard, and only that one: Platform.h's OS(UNIX) block also turns
    on WTF_USE_PTHREADS, HAVE_MMAP and <langinfo.h>, none of which we want.

    This is a wasm-only change. Off wasm the preprocessor sees the file
    unchanged.

UPSTREAM
    Not offered upstream: masm is a vendored fork of an old JavaScriptCore and
    Qt does not take wasi patches for it today. Would be a one-line addition to
    the OS(UNIX) list in Platform.h if it ever were.

CLASSIFICATION
    as-is -- the value is the true page size, not a stand-in.
--- a/src/3rdparty/masm/wtf/PageBlock.cpp
+++ b/src/3rdparty/masm/wtf/PageBlock.cpp
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 #include "config.h"
 #include "PageBlock.h"
 
-#if OS(UNIX)
+#if OS(UNIX) || defined(__wasi__)
 #include <unistd.h>
 #endif
 
@@ -40,7 +40,14 @@
 static size_t s_pageSize;
 static size_t s_pageMask;
 
-#if OS(UNIX)
+// wasi-libc is a Unix-like libc, but masm's Platform.h does not know the name:
+// its OS(UNIX) test is a fixed list of systems plus `defined(unix)`, and
+// wasi-sdk defines none of those. Adding WASI to OS(UNIX) wholesale is wrong --
+// that same block turns on WTF_USE_PTHREADS, HAVE_MMAP and <langinfo.h> -- so
+// only this one function is widened. sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE) IS in wasi-libc and
+// answers 65536, the wasm linear-memory page, which is what pageSize() wants
+// and is a power of two as pageSize()'s ASSERT requires.
+#if OS(UNIX) || defined(__wasi__)
 
 inline size_t systemPageSize()
 {
